{"type":"step-done","workflow":"build","step":"build-challenge","status":"DONE","at":"2026-11-19T09:10:11Z","parentSha":"f2f14d44a5a284d92483b913e5190d55004ff7ad","artifacts":["docs/plans/202611/logs/1031-pre-push-refuses/build-challenge-1.md","docs/plans/202611/logs/1031-pre-push-refuses/build-challenge-2.md"],"verdict":"CONCERNS","attempt":1,"failures":8,"round":1,"challengeFindings":[{"severity":"HIGH","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:678","title":"In bkit's own repo (`bkit.testing.minPushPaths: [\"docs/**\"]`) and in any repo whose `minPushPaths` covers `docs/templates/**`, a `[skip ci]` push to `main` that changes an audit template's project section passes `--target=main`: `mainAuditFiles` hands `paths` (with `minPushPaths`) to `minPushOutside`, the template matches a min-push path, never lands in `outside`, so it never reaches `sections` and is never refused"},{"severity":"MEDIUM","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:676","title":"A `[skip ci]` push to `main` carrying `docs/audits/202611/sécurité.md` (any non-ASCII, tab, double quote or backslash in the name) passes `min-push --target=main`, because `git diff --name-only` without `-z` prints the path C-quoted (`\"docs/audits/202611/s\\303\\251curit\\303\\251.md\"`), which fails `startsWith(\"docs/audits/\")`, while today's `-z` pathspec check still counts it as a min-push file"},{"severity":"MEDIUM","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:681","title":"After a `bkit upgrade` lands on `dev` (every audit template's managed block now differs from `origin/main`), a project-section edit pushed to `dev` under `[skip ci]` and then promoted to `main` under a `[skip ci]` plans-only head passes `--target=main`: against `origin/main` the template's managed head differs (or the template is new to `main`), so `minPushOutside` files it under `outside`, not `sections`, and `mainAuditFiles` only refuses `sections`. A template with more change than section-only escapes a check that refuses section-only"},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/templates/.husky/pre-push:246","title":"A `[skip ci]` push to `main` refused for code (`src/a.ts` outside the min-push paths), for an unresolved `origin/main` (exit 7) or for an older engine that rejects `--target` (`unknown flag --target`, exit 2) still prints \"Audit reports and audit-template project sections may skip CI on dev only ... (the files are named above)\", although no audit file was named; the hook keys the line on `push_target` being set, not on the refusal reason, and throws away the JSON `reason` on stdout"},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:748","title":"On the new `reason: \"audit\"` path, `min-push --json` puts the audit files in `outside` (files that DO match a min-push path, against the spec \"the changed files no min-push path matches\"), drops the real outside files of the same push, and mixes ranges: `changed` counts the `origin/dev` range while `outside` comes from the `origin/main` range, so in the \"already on origin/dev\" case `outside` names a file that `changed` never counted"},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:673","title":"A `[skip ci]` push of an audit report to `main` on a remote other than `origin` (for example `git push upstream HEAD:main` while the fork's `origin/main` already holds the report) passes, because the main check measures from the local `origin/main` ref and not from the `main` SHA the pushed-to remote advertises on the hook's stdin"}]}
