{"type":"step-done","workflow":"build","step":"build-challenge","status":"DONE","at":"2026-11-19T10:22:32Z","parentSha":"b7dc3503883bec085bd485c71266f246e61eb51a","artifacts":["docs/plans/202611/logs/1031-pre-push-refuses/build-challenge-1.md","docs/plans/202611/logs/1031-pre-push-refuses/build-challenge-2.md"],"verdict":"CONCERNS","attempt":2,"failures":4,"round":2,"challengeFindings":[{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:672","title":"In a repo whose `minPushPaths` covers `docs/templates/**` (bkit's own `docs/**`), a `[skip ci]` push to `main` that adds a project-written `docs/templates/bkit-audit-custom.md` with no bkit markers, or edits an audit template whose managed block does not parse (CRLF line endings, a second line-anchored `<!-- bkit:end -->` in the project section), passes `--target=main`: `projectSection` maps a null `managedHead` to `\"\"`, so both sides compare as an empty project section and the file is never refused"},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:692","title":"A `[skip ci]` push to `main` whose changed audit template cannot be read at the pushed commit (a `spawnSync` error such as `EAGAIN` or `ENOBUFS`, a failed lazy blob fetch in a `--filter=blob:none` clone, or a non-blob entry at the path) passes `--target=main` in a repo whose `minPushPaths` covers it: `projectSection` turns every non-zero `cat-file` status into \"absent\", and `mainAuditFiles` treats an absent pushed side as a deletion, so a read failure fails open where today's `minPushOutside` fails closed"},{"severity":"LOW","location":".bkit/core/engine/commands/ci/ci.ts:683","title":"A `[skip ci]` push of `docs/audits/202611/security.md` to `main` passes `min-push --target=main` (exit 0, `minPush: true`) when the checkout holds a local branch or tag named `origin/main` at the pushed commit (`git checkout -b origin/main`, `git tag origin/main`), because `mainAuditFiles` passes the bare name `origin/main` to `rev-parse` and `merge-base`, git resolves it as `refs/tags/origin/main` or `refs/heads/origin/main` before `refs/remotes/origin/main`, so the merge-base is the pushed commit itself and the audit diff is empty"}]}
